---
// **The four things somebody should know before they commit to this race**, in one place
// because both pages that need them need exactly these four.
//
// `/nn/` shows them as *what this race is*, above the interest form. `/nn/2026/` shows them as
// *what you are about to enter*, above the entry form. Two copies of four safety-relevant
// bullets is two copies that drift, and the one that would drift is the one nobody re-read —
// so there is one copy, here.
//
// ## What is deliberately not in it
//
// **A time.** The bullet used to end "everybody walks down together at 10:30", and 10:30 is a
// row in this year's schedule rather than a property of the race. It is on
// `/nn/<year>/race-day/`, in the schedule the committee edits, and this says the part that is
// true whichever year it is: you do not have to find the start on your own.
//
// **A distance from HQ to the start.** Nobody has supplied one, and deriving it from the
// coordinates and a guessed school entrance is exactly the plausible-looking number this
// repository keeps out of markup. See the note in `2026/race-day.astro`.
//
// Every line here is the club's own 2023 copy and is **draft pending committee approval**,
// like the rest of these pages.
---

<ul class="nn-arrows">
  <li>
    A tough, properly off-road course — uneven, rocky, rooty, and slippery when wet.
    <strong>Trail shoes recommended</strong>, road shoes acceptable.
  </li>
  <li><strong>No headphones of any type during the race.</strong></li>
  <li>One water station on the route, one at the finish, and marshals throughout.</li>
  <li>
    <strong>The start and the finish are not at race HQ.</strong> Everybody walks down together
    beforehand, so there is nothing to find on your own.
  </li>
</ul>
